From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] output: show the largest uncovered client buffer on a hardware
 plane

On a GPU that can barely composite its screen, as the Mali-450 at
2256x1504, compositing a browser's page every frame costs 17 ms of a
33 ms budget. The display hardware can show that buffer on an overlay
plane and scale it there, at no GPU cost.

Each frame, the largest opaque dmabuf client buffer that nothing above
it covers, and that fills at least an eighth of the output, is taken
out of composition onto an output layer. An opaque rect stands in its
place in the scene, so what lies beneath it, as the window a page is
part of, damages nothing when it repaints. The surface's commits
schedule frames and it hears its frames done, as composited ones do.
A buffer the backend does not accept is composited again from the next
frame and not offered again at that size.

Output layers need the DRM backend's libliftoff interface, so this
works only with WLR_DRM_FORCE_LIBLIFTOFF set; otherwise nothing
changes.

Signed-off-by: Artem Butusov <art.sormy@gmail.com>
---
--- a/include/labwc.h
+++ b/include/labwc.h
@@ -423,6 +423,7 @@
 
 	bool leased;
 	bool gamma_lut_changed;
+	struct output_planes *planes;
 };
 
 #undef LAB_NR_LAYERS
--- a/include/output-planes.h
+++ b/include/output-planes.h
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+/* SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only */
+#ifndef LABWC_OUTPUT_PLANES_H
+#define LABWC_OUTPUT_PLANES_H
+
+#include <stdbool.h>
+#include <time.h>
+
+struct output;
+struct wlr_output_state;
+
+/*
+ * One client buffer shown by the display hardware on a plane of its own,
+ * instead of composited by the GPU: the largest opaque dmabuf on the output
+ * that nothing covers, as a browser's page or a video. Needs the DRM backend's
+ * libliftoff interface (WLR_DRM_FORCE_LIBLIFTOFF), the only one that takes
+ * output layers; without it, nothing changes.
+ */
+void output_planes_init(struct output *output);
+void output_planes_finish(struct output *output);
+
+/* Before the frame is built: takes a buffer out of composition onto the plane */
+void output_planes_prepare(struct output *output, struct wlr_output_state *state);
+
+/*
+ * After the frame is committed, when the backend says whether it took the
+ * layer: a refused buffer is composited again from the next frame
+ */
+void output_planes_committed(struct output *output);
+
+/* The plane's surface hears its frames were shown, as composited ones do */
+void output_planes_send_frame_done(struct output *output, const struct timespec *now);
+
+#endif /* LABWC_OUTPUT_PLANES_H */
